{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "01KA", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-valuative-criterion-universal-closedness}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:53cacf8d91589cc8724471a1aa1746510c5c12314d85dcdc333b8f55372b7a38", "source_text": "Valuative criterion for universal closedness", "source_text_hash": "sha256:85c056d729d7c8bf2bb01ccc241dc6e4f689db1daa920a8b761a38e411e32df7", "unit_id": "tag:01KA:title"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01KA", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{topology-section-proper}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:54d1fecb6760682572f8bbbfab45eccb026aad4c10e1ac303a6e1a06be8141c2", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn Topology, Section <REF_0001> there is a\ndiscussion of proper maps as closed maps of topological spaces\nall of whose fibres are quasi-compact, or as maps such that\nall base changes are closed maps. Here is the corresponding notion\nin algebraic geometry.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9bab266d56f5c21d67d2211a8e69315bc55e9c7af92103b3780b7b18508d3bdf", "unit_id": "tag:01KA:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01KA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f' : X_{S'} \\to S'$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-universally-closed}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:22f1143a91bbc5b2dc1cc872d56d9821fdee1f1167727e8710157fadeca643db", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:01e624ae4a0347b2178110953f06d8d5e73cba7d2d4ffe6a190d88e50684379c", "source_text": "A morphism of schemes <MATH_0001> is said to be\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001>universally closed<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if every base change\n<MATH_0002> is closed.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e961b21d6567c9f1f63db0613e74df22a7274436c2a819c2738ae1d9cc6e46ad", "unit_id": "tag:01KB:statement"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01KA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0002": "$X \\to S$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "MATH_0004": "$X_{S'} \\to S'$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{P}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-section-proper}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4c0bdaf20d7997309f9a0d3872673c6bb87841e2ae0f81bae6aa36112342d093", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9cb6eb32659fcae4ee7b5196153d23a29cfdf1d44e13bd9573fa62835e36d4bc", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn fact the adjective ``universally'' is often used in this way.\nIn other words, given a property <MATH_0001> of morphisms\nthen we say that ``<MATH_0002> is universally <MATH_0003>''\nif and only if every base change <MATH_0004> has <MATH_0005>.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nPlease take a look at Morphisms, Section <REF_0001> for a\nmore detailed discussion of the properties of universally closed morphisms.\nIn this section we restrict the discussion to the relationship between\nuniversal closed morphisms and morphisms satisfying the\nexistence part of the valuative criterion.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:698d51552107cdfcaab6301505b98989c29fdd24b44085cde86331b7e081bdbc", "unit_id": "tag:01KA:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01KA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topology-definition-lift-specializations}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-specializations-lift}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:bc73fce741f7c13a43e11f39958a5c077fa460834d787b3cf27908cf2861800c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cc82461f10b961b49540104f6930b63eff681e688bc98da337b818fc7780f596", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0002> is universally closed then specializations lift\nalong any base change of <MATH_0003>, see\nTopology, Definition <REF_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0004> is quasi-compact and specializations lift\nalong any base change of <MATH_0005>, then <MATH_0006> is universally closed.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c250905835bc4069188bdf02f4cac9fc01db3440703cfe50481e8c1ec197d414", "unit_id": "tag:01KC:statement"}
